WEBVTT

00:12.390 --> 00:14.870
You're eating that fish like you're fighting with it.

00:23.310 --> 00:24.020
Fish...

00:24.840 --> 00:27.920
My home is by the sea, and the fish there are quite delicious.

00:27.920 --> 00:31.870
Yes, Shounan is your hometown, isn't it?

00:32.260 --> 00:36.720
The dried fish there are great, but butterfish are the best.

00:37.050 --> 00:38.220
How nice...

00:38.220 --> 00:41.300
I envy you since there are no lakes in Biei.

00:41.300 --> 00:42.250
I see...

00:43.070 --> 00:45.730
Biei is in the middle of Hokkaido, after all.

00:45.730 --> 00:46.310
Yes.

00:46.310 --> 00:48.670
But the food isn't that bad up there either!

00:48.950 --> 00:50.840
Hokkaido is huge!

00:48.950 --> 00:53.460
"Hokkaido ha dekkaido" is a Japanese joke.

00:48.950 --> 00:53.460
Dekkaido (dekkai kaido) means large sea route, and is a pun on Hokkaido.

00:51.460 --> 00:53.460
What kind of phrase is that?

00:53.930 --> 00:56.450
Hokkaido's Kegani crab is the best.

00:56.510 --> 00:57.820
Yeah!

00:57.820 --> 00:59.950
Their crab miso is the best.

00:59.950 --> 01:01.490
The best, indeed!

03:08.820 --> 03:10.240
Ah, Sora-chan.

03:10.240 --> 03:11.650
You can go on ahead now.

03:21.650 --> 03:23.210
You broke the lock?

03:23.830 --> 03:24.740
That's all?

03:24.940 --> 03:25.590
Yeah.

03:26.060 --> 03:29.090
You can do that even without magic, right?

03:29.090 --> 03:30.340
Really?

03:30.630 --> 03:34.010
It doesn't seem like the type of magic that Suzuki Sora would do, though.

03:34.010 --> 03:36.180
More like...

03:36.570 --> 03:40.020
using outrageous magic is what makes you Suzuki Sora!

03:40.950 --> 03:43.060
Sounds like we made her angry.

03:43.060 --> 03:44.070
It does, doesn't it?

03:45.890 --> 03:48.110
So what's everyone here talking about?

03:48.670 --> 03:49.750
Nothing much.

03:50.360 --> 03:53.790
Hiyori-chan, how did the magic training you were so worried about go?

03:54.370 --> 04:00.410
Umm, my instructor was an old man, but he was really kind.

04:00.410 --> 04:02.450
Somehow I managed to do it well.

04:02.760 --> 04:04.030
Isn't that great?

04:04.210 --> 04:04.860
Yup!

04:05.190 --> 04:06.460
How about you, Midorikawa-kun?

04:10.280 --> 04:12.940
Well, everyone has their own forte.

04:13.890 --> 04:15.650
Good morning, everyone.

04:14.820 --> 04:16.790
Good morning.

04:16.950 --> 04:21.510
Today's lecture is about how mages were acknowledged in society,

04:21.510 --> 04:24.180
and how it has changed throughout history.

04:24.680 --> 04:29.060
In ancient times, mankind always lived in fear of death...

04:30.490 --> 04:32.050
Hey, Gouta.

04:32.050 --> 04:33.310
Is that your second one?

04:33.310 --> 04:33.980
Yeah.

04:34.250 --> 04:35.790
It's delicious!

04:36.590 --> 04:41.120
Your mom is amazing, making these two awesome lunchboxes.

04:41.310 --> 04:44.350
I eat the first one as my breakfast since I get really hungry after surfing.

04:49.380 --> 04:51.540
At my house, breakfast is from a convenience store...

04:51.760 --> 04:52.370
Isn't that alright?

04:52.370 --> 04:53.350
You can eat whatever you like.

04:53.640 --> 04:55.120
Then let's switch!

04:55.870 --> 04:56.530
No way.

04:58.260 --> 05:00.690
Nomiya-san, have you met Gouta's mother?

05:01.320 --> 05:02.800
She came to the PTA meeting, right?

05:02.800 --> 05:05.060
She's such a babe!

05:05.420 --> 05:08.440
Nomiya's mother is like a traditional Enka singer...

05:09.070 --> 05:11.140
Your mom is a sumo wrestler!

05:11.140 --> 05:13.030
Man, you guys are noisy.

05:13.370 --> 05:15.470
Gouta-kun's fried shrimp, mine now!

05:16.060 --> 05:17.020
Look!

05:16.770 --> 05:18.300
Konichi, you bastard!

05:18.050 --> 05:18.760
Save me.

05:30.720 --> 05:31.850
I'm back.

05:34.980 --> 05:36.930
I'll get started on dinner right away.

05:40.300 --> 05:41.150
You know...

05:42.550 --> 05:43.400
What?

05:43.720 --> 05:45.630
Is there something you want to eat?

05:46.470 --> 05:48.440
Your lunchbox was really yummy.

05:48.710 --> 05:51.900
Well now, hearing something nice from you all of a sudden.

05:52.800 --> 05:54.330
Today was a really weird day.

05:54.770 --> 05:59.020
Your father messaged me today, saying my lunchbox was delicious too.

06:00.780 --> 06:03.080
I guess a parent and child are really alike.

06:03.860 --> 06:05.660
Perhaps it's in the blood.

06:07.030 --> 06:08.900
Both of you are weird in the same way.

06:08.900 --> 06:09.780
Huh?

06:09.780 --> 06:10.950
Give me a break.

06:12.340 --> 06:13.410
Midorikawa-kun.

06:13.990 --> 06:14.640
Yes.

06:18.580 --> 06:23.190
As expected from Gouta-sensei, you were able to get an 89 in that subject matter.

06:23.590 --> 06:26.130
Not really, it wasn't as good as I expected.

06:26.130 --> 06:28.420
I hate you.

06:28.650 --> 06:30.720
If it was my family, we'd be celebrating with red bean rice.

06:28.650 --> 06:33.020
Red Bean rice is served at special occassions; marriage, new years etc.

06:30.720 --> 06:33.020
So you're finally a man now, huh?

06:33.200 --> 06:35.090
How nice it is to be smart!

06:35.090 --> 06:37.140
And to have such a beautiful mother, too!

06:37.140 --> 06:39.470
That has nothing to do with this.

06:39.470 --> 06:41.520
Want to switch mothers with me?

06:41.760 --> 06:42.540
Idiot.

06:42.680 --> 06:45.730
Then switch your brain with mine!

06:45.730 --> 06:46.630
Stupid!

06:46.850 --> 06:47.740
Midorikawa-kun.

06:49.000 --> 06:49.890
Midorikawa-kun.

06:51.000 --> 06:52.650
Midorikawa-kun!

06:53.990 --> 06:57.200
It's your choice whether you want to listen to the lecture or not.

06:57.530 --> 07:02.750
However, I request that you don't disturb other students who are paying attention.

07:05.140 --> 07:06.370
I apologize.

07:14.000 --> 07:17.880
Recently, I feel like I'm out of luck.

07:18.620 --> 07:20.390
Did something happen at the Magic Bureau?

07:22.710 --> 07:25.260
This will be your place for magic training today.

07:25.850 --> 07:28.750
The client inside is Aimoto Eiji-san, age 32.

07:29.110 --> 07:30.730
He works as a freewriter

07:30.900 --> 07:35.000
and his request is for us to search for his lost insurance card.

07:37.930 --> 07:41.200
Yeah I can't find it. You two can really help me out there.

07:41.650 --> 07:43.090
Try to be quick about it.

07:44.980 --> 07:50.070
Today's request is to find your lost insurance card, right?

07:50.390 --> 07:54.700
Look, can't you just use magic to clean this place up?

07:55.150 --> 07:57.760
You could easily find the card that way.

07:59.270 --> 08:01.560
It's fine as long as we just find the insurance card, right?

08:02.970 --> 08:06.640
Like I said, clean up the place first!

08:07.150 --> 08:09.770
If you do that, it'll appear naturally.

08:15.470 --> 08:16.520
Ah, Miharu-chan?

08:17.340 --> 08:18.380
Heh, I see.

08:18.640 --> 08:21.860
He was blabbering around, something about getting all fired up tonight.

08:22.820 --> 08:24.470
Ah, that's right.

08:24.970 --> 08:25.660
What?

08:25.660 --> 08:26.820
You're going too?

08:26.820 --> 08:27.620
Okay.

08:27.620 --> 08:28.550
Aimoto-san!

08:28.920 --> 08:31.700
The request does not mention cleaning up your room.

08:32.010 --> 08:35.970
As such, we will use magic only to find the insurance card.

08:38.220 --> 08:39.380
Sorry, sorry!

08:39.380 --> 08:41.580
I have guests over right now.

08:41.750 --> 08:43.860
They don't seem to understand Japanese, so it's a bother.

08:45.390 --> 08:47.540
Yeah, hold on for a second.

08:48.850 --> 08:51.760
Like I said, you'll find it if you clean up!

08:52.320 --> 08:54.330
Should be easy if you can use magic.

08:54.540 --> 08:55.560
That guy...

08:56.030 --> 08:57.520
Well, sorry.

08:57.520 --> 09:00.480
Things just keep piling up, you know.

09:00.480 --> 09:01.650
It's a real pain in the neck.

09:02.060 --> 09:03.730
Ah, as I was saying...

09:03.730 --> 09:07.550
What you're saying is different from what was in the request.

09:08.120 --> 09:09.490
What is with that boy?

09:09.990 --> 09:12.950
Oh, a few mages have come over to my place.

09:13.070 --> 09:15.250
But they all have problems understanding me.

09:15.640 --> 09:16.830
Hang up the phone!

09:17.460 --> 09:18.120
Huh?

09:18.260 --> 09:19.080
Gouta-kun!

09:19.590 --> 09:21.540
Is that the kind of attitude you have when you're talking with other people?

09:22.170 --> 09:23.330
Hang up the phone!

09:23.800 --> 09:25.460
What is with you and your attitude?

09:35.150 --> 09:36.140
Wait!

09:37.000 --> 09:40.390
Do you always run away the moment it gets difficult?

09:41.340 --> 09:43.210
There are many types of people in this world.

09:43.500 --> 09:46.360
If you keep running away, you won't be able to survive in this world!

09:47.920 --> 09:48.910
If that's how it is...

09:49.650 --> 09:52.260
then I don't need this world.

09:53.720 --> 09:55.570
Summer break training...

09:55.730 --> 09:56.550
what do you mean?

09:56.930 --> 10:00.790
I didn't know anything about your father being a mage either...

10:02.540 --> 10:04.210
My old man is a mage?

10:05.000 --> 10:07.490
I never heard of that.

10:08.070 --> 10:09.180
I'm sorry.

10:10.460 --> 10:14.070
I was deceived too, for seventeen years!

10:14.530 --> 10:15.630
What is this about?

10:16.460 --> 10:17.590
I failed...

10:18.040 --> 10:19.860
I gave up on magic.

10:20.300 --> 10:22.130
I wasn't able to use it properly...

10:22.510 --> 10:24.310
That is no reason to hide it!

10:24.310 --> 10:28.120
No matter how sudden this may have been to Gouta, even he could have made his own decision...

10:27.560 --> 10:28.120
I...

10:28.800 --> 10:30.610
But I couldn't tell you...

10:30.800 --> 10:31.780
Why not?

10:31.780 --> 10:32.490
Because...

10:34.010 --> 10:37.820
Because I knew that you hated mages...

10:37.820 --> 10:38.950
What's that supposed to mean?

10:41.050 --> 10:45.700
You were silly yet honest, and could talk to anyone truthfully...

10:45.700 --> 10:47.560
I liked you for that.

10:47.950 --> 10:48.940
I'm sorry.

10:49.750 --> 10:52.920
I can't live with a liar.

10:53.430 --> 10:54.460
Gouta, what will you do?

10:55.090 --> 10:57.520
Mama is going to go to grandmother's place in Naga.

10:58.460 --> 10:59.190
I...

10:59.670 --> 11:00.760
Make up your mind now.

11:00.760 --> 11:01.760
I can't...

11:01.760 --> 11:03.530
telling me to suddenly decide where to go.

11:03.890 --> 11:05.290
I still have school.

11:06.020 --> 11:06.770
I see.

11:06.770 --> 11:09.610
Then I'll go by myself.

11:10.450 --> 11:11.490
I'm sorry.

11:13.680 --> 11:16.750
You take care of yourself.

11:22.540 --> 11:25.060
Pops, why aren't you going after her?

11:25.440 --> 11:26.890
Mom is leaving us!

11:27.270 --> 11:29.600
I'm a liar...

11:30.510 --> 11:33.220
I'm sorry, Kazumi...

11:33.430 --> 11:34.210
I...

11:34.210 --> 11:35.010
Pops...

11:40.180 --> 11:41.430
Hey, did you hear?

11:41.610 --> 11:44.540
Midorikawa-kun is a mage.

11:45.210 --> 11:47.510
If you get close to him, he'll cast magic on you.

11:47.670 --> 11:49.240
Scary!

11:50.380 --> 11:52.100
Stop saying those things.

11:52.100 --> 11:52.810
Huh?

11:53.180 --> 11:55.390
He's been hiding it from us until now.

11:56.050 --> 11:59.900
I bet he used magic on that test, that's why he did so well, right?

11:59.900 --> 12:00.970
Stop it.

12:01.510 --> 12:02.980
Aren't you scared too?

12:07.120 --> 12:09.200
Ah, Konishi, hurry up with lunch!

12:09.200 --> 12:10.120
Let's go play soccer.

12:10.560 --> 12:11.250
Okay.

12:11.360 --> 12:12.790
Gouta, are you coming?

12:12.470 --> 12:14.180
Who's Gouta?

12:14.360 --> 12:15.380
Hey, Nomiya!

12:15.580 --> 12:18.380
We don't have any friends who are mages, do we?

12:25.520 --> 12:30.180
Well, I didn't intend to cause a scene either.

12:31.200 --> 12:34.560
We still found the insurance card, after all.

12:35.430 --> 12:37.300
And the room is clean too.

12:37.730 --> 12:40.880
Really, I didn't want to fight.

12:41.390 --> 12:43.270
Can't you guys stop bowing?

12:43.270 --> 12:44.140
You know...

12:44.300 --> 12:46.010
You put up with him pretty well.

12:46.800 --> 12:47.530
Yeah.

12:48.090 --> 12:51.650
But you know, not every client is like that.

12:53.260 --> 12:57.130
There are all kinds of people, but a lot of them are nice.

12:57.410 --> 12:58.000
Yes.

12:59.100 --> 13:01.550
I'm glad you endured through it today.

13:07.470 --> 13:09.290
Sora-chan!

13:09.700 --> 13:11.790
Sora-chan!

13:13.460 --> 13:15.160
Sorry, did you wait long?

13:15.620 --> 13:17.360
Not really, it's all right.

13:17.800 --> 13:19.580
It's really hot today.

13:27.330 --> 13:28.170
A kimono?

13:28.500 --> 13:30.860
I study Japanese dance.

13:30.860 --> 13:31.930
Japanese dance...

13:32.580 --> 13:33.630
Unexpected, isn't it?

13:37.710 --> 13:39.830
Ah, such a cute yukata!

13:39.830 --> 13:41.930
Look, look, Sora-chan!

13:52.210 --> 13:53.070
What do you think?

13:53.450 --> 13:56.840
Good, it has a lot of electronic sounds, and it was very entertaining.

13:56.840 --> 13:57.770
Thanks.

13:58.430 --> 14:00.970
This kind of music is pretty uncommon though.

14:00.970 --> 14:04.370
I like the New Wave music from England.

14:05.300 --> 14:07.700
I'll listen to your recommendations next time.

14:08.020 --> 14:08.690
Okay!

14:22.470 --> 14:23.330
Father...

14:27.330 --> 14:28.260
What are you doing?

14:29.260 --> 14:30.750
Just taking a rest.

14:31.340 --> 14:32.060
I see.

14:33.130 --> 14:34.040
Where are you going?

14:35.500 --> 14:36.200
Going out to eat.

14:36.610 --> 14:38.160
You're not going to eat with everyone?

14:38.710 --> 14:39.730
How do I put it...

14:40.220 --> 14:42.720
I just wanted to go out and eat conveyor belt sushi.

14:44.070 --> 14:47.810
Don't you think that's a bit strange, seeing sushi that goes around?

14:48.320 --> 14:49.850
Stop following me, then.

14:49.850 --> 14:53.170
Spin, spin, Suzuki is spinning!

14:55.220 --> 14:56.300
What the...

15:04.810 --> 15:06.830
Ah, it's the woman with the guitar again!

15:46.300 --> 15:47.450
Umm...

15:49.660 --> 15:52.090
Hey, wait up!

16:01.020 --> 16:03.420
That was great, Yasuko-chan.

16:03.460 --> 16:04.520
Thank you.

16:03.460 --> 16:04.920
The best, the best!

16:05.740 --> 16:07.920
Let's see, what should I sing next...

16:09.730 --> 16:10.590
You know...

16:12.010 --> 16:13.640
Don't tell me, this is your first time...

16:16.660 --> 16:17.320
Yes.

16:19.970 --> 16:20.730
Thank you for your patronage.

16:24.040 --> 16:25.730
It's so delicious!

16:25.730 --> 16:27.360
You really are amazing.

16:27.360 --> 16:28.500
Huh, about what?

16:29.050 --> 16:30.090
Oh, nothing.

16:30.260 --> 16:31.740
Mister, keep them coming!

16:31.740 --> 16:32.400
All right!

16:44.400 --> 16:45.500
Interesting, wasn't it?

16:45.890 --> 16:46.550
Huh?

16:47.030 --> 16:48.530
Yesterday's conveyor belt sushi.

16:48.690 --> 16:52.160
Ah, I ate too much.

16:52.470 --> 16:55.400
Really, although you're small, you can eat a lot.

16:58.340 --> 16:59.990
Yesterday was a lot of fun.

17:00.000 --> 17:00.640
Yeah!

17:01.190 --> 17:02.780
What did you guys do?

17:03.090 --> 17:05.970
Hiyo-chan came to Shimokita to visit.

17:06.770 --> 17:08.610
Call me next time too.

17:08.970 --> 17:09.620
Huh?

17:10.210 --> 17:12.590
Next time, it'll be the three of us!

17:13.770 --> 17:15.800
Ah, sounds like fun!

17:35.950 --> 17:40.890
Today's client is Takenaka Yuuko-san, age 31, who works as a translator...

17:40.150 --> 17:40.890
I...

17:41.250 --> 17:43.810
still can't perform magic at all.

17:44.560 --> 17:48.220
Therefore, I would like you to perform the magic properly in my stead, please.

17:48.490 --> 17:49.520
Gouta-kun.

17:50.790 --> 17:54.510
I probably wrote down everything I could remember,  but...

17:55.250 --> 17:59.220
Your request stated that it was sweet, round and pasty.

17:59.580 --> 18:03.080
It was covered with a gentleness that holds you in.

18:03.610 --> 18:08.080
It's impossible to find it with such a vague description, isn't it?

18:08.930 --> 18:11.380
But that's why you're relying on mages, right?

18:11.890 --> 18:15.290
Yes, I would really like to drink it again.

18:16.340 --> 18:19.180
I've been trying to remember that taste these days.

18:20.660 --> 18:23.470
Let's see, what kind of magic should we use?

18:23.670 --> 18:24.340
Umm...

18:24.790 --> 18:25.890
Have you thought of something?

18:26.540 --> 18:27.760
That suitcase...

18:28.650 --> 18:29.610
Are you going on a trip?

18:30.730 --> 18:33.260
No, I'll be staying at the hospital.

18:34.640 --> 18:36.840
I may be gone for a while.

18:38.940 --> 18:42.130
A drink that is sweet and round and has a kind of gentleness...

18:42.610 --> 18:43.270
Yes,

18:43.700 --> 18:45.860
it makes you feel comfortable.

18:46.670 --> 18:48.410
I think you should try giving her mother's...

18:51.090 --> 18:52.320
I see.

18:53.400 --> 18:54.930
I've decided on the magic.

18:55.410 --> 18:56.790
I'm counting on you.

18:58.680 --> 19:00.080
A warm heart,

19:00.400 --> 19:01.750
the power of kindness,

19:02.100 --> 19:05.570
please appear in the middle of this cup!

19:19.110 --> 19:19.770
Please.

19:20.230 --> 19:20.980
Yes.

19:29.430 --> 19:30.810
What is this horrible...

19:31.210 --> 19:33.210
I asked for something sweet...

19:35.410 --> 19:36.060
Oh?

19:44.470 --> 19:45.380
I see...

19:45.790 --> 19:51.440
this taste, it's a bit mysterious but it's nostalgic.

19:51.670 --> 19:53.740
What is this?

19:54.540 --> 19:55.540
It's mother's milk.

19:55.770 --> 19:56.800
Mother's milk?

19:57.510 --> 20:00.700
When I heard your words, Yuuko-san,

20:00.990 --> 20:03.480
I remembered what my mother said to me.

20:05.230 --> 20:09.660
"At times when you were feeding, I would always try some of my own milk."

20:11.110 --> 20:13.510
Then she'd say it would taste terrible.

20:14.750 --> 20:16.780
But she felt that within that taste,

20:16.780 --> 20:20.080
it contained the strength needed to raise a baby.

20:20.080 --> 20:20.800
Yes.

20:21.450 --> 20:25.190
Regardless if it was sweet or round, it was a kind feeling.

20:25.520 --> 20:26.170
Yes.

20:26.820 --> 20:28.860
It was a comforting and dearing taste.

20:29.910 --> 20:32.280
Thank you very much for letting me remember it.

20:33.270 --> 20:33.930
Not at all.

20:35.090 --> 20:37.230
I have breast cancer.

20:37.970 --> 20:39.630
I see now...

20:39.770 --> 20:44.110
I must have been thinking about my mother who passed away.

20:44.680 --> 20:45.820
Please don't give up.

20:46.690 --> 20:50.150
I won't, because my mother has always encouraged me.

20:50.780 --> 20:54.580
I hope I can have a successful surgery and be able to come back.

20:56.140 --> 21:01.270
Your mother must have been a wonderful person to raise a son like you.

21:02.540 --> 21:03.380
Thank you,

21:04.520 --> 21:05.410
it was delicious.

21:09.570 --> 21:10.870
They're large, aren't they?

21:11.670 --> 21:13.920
These goldfish are really large.

21:14.710 --> 21:18.420
Sayori-san's daughter caught these at the festival.

21:18.820 --> 21:20.920
She has a daughter?

21:21.950 --> 21:23.880
She left home after a fight.

21:24.420 --> 21:25.660
It's already been three years.

21:26.100 --> 21:27.250
Three years...

21:28.130 --> 21:32.600
These goldfishes are very dear to Sayori-san.

23:06.090 --> 23:10.700
If there was a spell to warm people's hearts, that kind of magic would be great.

23:11.040 --> 23:13.950
But you can't expect everything to go smoothly...

23:14.530 --> 23:16.210
Next time, Shimokitazawa.

23:16.620 --> 23:19.620
Hara-sensei has played Rock & Roll before, you know!
